            <ArticleTitle>Gastroesophageal reflux disease and airway hyperresponsiveness: concomitance beyond the realm of chance?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>680-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1806-37132011000500017</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastroesophageal reflux disease and asthma are both quite common the world over, and they can coexist. However, the nature of the relationship between these two diseases remains unclear. In this study, we review controversial aspects of the relationships among asthma, airway hyperresponsiveness, and gastroesophageal reflux disease in adults and in children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
